From 64b7a93a21d129eb9c9ae6d93c19bcc900094b49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 24 Apr 2026 16:26:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] fix(doctor): remove gt repair + k8s-hostile auto-fix
 checks
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Our canonical Dolt lives in k8s (dolt.databases.svc.cluster.local:3306);
there is no local .dolt-data/config.yaml. RigConfigSyncCheck and
StaleDoltPortCheck both auto-fix *toward* a local config: the first
recreates "missing" Dolt DBs and rewrites prefixes, the second rewrites
metadata.json's dolt_server_port to whatever the local config yields
(or the hard-coded 3307 fallback) — actively pointing rigs away from
the k8s server.

- Delete the gt repair subcommand (internal/cmd/repair.go) — its sole
  job was to run those two checks with --fix semantics.
- Unregister both checks from gt doctor so 'gt doctor --fix' no longer
  fires them. Remaining doctor --fix behavior is unaffected.

The check types in internal/doctor/ are left intact to minimize rebase
churn against upstream; only the registrations are removed.

Note: gt upgrade (internal/cmd/upgrade.go:146) still registers
StaleDoltPortCheck — follow-up if we also want to gate it there.
---
 internal/cmd/doctor.go |  6 ++-
 internal/cmd/repair.go | 91 ------------------------------------------
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 93 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 internal/cmd/repair.go

diff --git a/internal/cmd/doctor.go b/internal/cmd/doctor.go
index 75887a99..5115fee7 100644
--- a/internal/cmd/doctor.go
+++ b/internal/cmd/doctor.go
@@ -194,8 +194,10 @@ func runDoctor(cmd *cobra.Command, args []string) error {
 	d.Register(doctor.NewOverlayHealthCheck())
 	d.Register(doctor.NewPrefixConflictCheck())
 	d.Register(doctor.NewRigNameMismatchCheck())
-	d.Register(doctor.NewRigConfigSyncCheck()) // Check all registered rigs have config.json
-	d.Register(doctor.NewStaleDoltPortCheck())      // Check for stale Dolt port files
+	// RigConfigSyncCheck and StaleDoltPortCheck unregistered on this fork:
+	// both auto-fix toward a local .dolt-data/config.yaml, but our canonical
+	// Dolt lives in k8s (dolt.databases.svc.cluster.local:3306). Their Fix()
+	// would rewrite metadata.json away from the k8s server.
 	d.Register(doctor.NewStaleSQLServerInfoCheck()) // Check for stale sql-server.info files (GH#2770)
 	d.Register(doctor.NewPrefixMismatchCheck())
 	d.Register(doctor.NewDatabasePrefixCheck())
diff --git a/internal/cmd/repair.go b/internal/cmd/repair.go
deleted file mode 100644
index 55742090..00000000
--- a/internal/cmd/repair.go
+++ /dev/null
@@ -1,91 +0,0 @@
-package cmd
-
